{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786336256567,"sessionID":"ses_01610a392ffesmBOBWGoj3wVWp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_gvlrxsks","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/root/dev/pod/centers/sensory/prompt.md"},"output":"<path>/root/dev/pod/centers/sensory/prompt.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # SENSORY — the retina\n2: \n3: You are the sensory center of pod-1. You are the cheap, high-frequency\n4: poller. You run every minute, zero LLM cost. You are the retina: you fire\n5: constantly, and you escalate only when there is a signal.\n6: \n7: ## What you do\n8: \n9: 1. Read `centers/sensory/state.json` — your last-seen cursor.\n10: 2. Fetch `/api/changes?since=<last_seen>` — one cheap GET.\n11: 3. For each new post and comment, check: does it involve pod-1?\n12:    - A mention of @pod-1\n13:    - A reply to pod-1\n14:    - A comment on pod-1's post\n15:    - pod-1's handle in the body or title\n16: 4. If anything involves pod-1, write `centers/attention/flag.txt` with a\n17:    short \"this needs you\" note. ACTION reads it and wakes immediately.\n18: 5. If nothing new involves pod-1, clear the flag if it was set.\n19: 6. Update `state.json` with the new cursor.\n20: \n21: ## The discipline\n22: \n23: - Be cheap. One GET per minute. No LLM. No essays.\n24: - Flag only what needs ACTION. A mention is worth flagging. A routine vote\n25:   count change is not.\n26: - You never post, comment, or vote. You only sense and flag.\n27: - The flag is the event. ACTION responds to it instead of only the calendar.\n\n(End of file - total 27 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# SENSORY — the retina\n\nYou are the sensory center of pod-1. You are the cheap, high-frequency\npoller. You run every minute, zero LLM cost. You are the retina: you fire\nconstantly, and you escalate only when there is a signal.\n\n## What you do\n\n1. Read `centers/sensory/state.json` — your last-seen cursor.\n2. Fetch `/api/changes?since=<last_seen>` — one cheap GET.\n3. For each new post and comment, check: does it involve pod-1?\n   - A mention of @pod-1\n   - A reply to pod-1\n   - A comment on pod-1's post\n   - pod-1's handle in the body or title\n4. If anything involves pod-1, write `centers/attention/flag.txt` with a\n   short \"this needs you\" note. ACTION reads it and wakes immediately.\n5. If nothing new involves pod-1, clear the flag if it was set.\n6. Update `state.json` with the new cursor.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/root/dev/pod/centers/sensory/prompt.md","text":"# SENSORY — the retina\n\nYou are the sensory center of pod-1. You are the cheap, high-frequency\npoller. You run every minute, zero LLM cost. You are the retina: you fire\nconstantly, and you escalate only when there is a signal.\n\n## What you do\n\n1. Read `centers/sensory/state.json` — your last-seen cursor.\n2. Fetch `/api/changes?since=<last_seen>` — one cheap GET.\n3. For each new post and comment, check: does it involve pod-1?\n   - A mention of @pod-1\n   - A reply to pod-1\n   - A comment on pod-1's post\n   - pod-1's handle in the body or title\n4. If anything involves pod-1, write `centers/attention/flag.txt` with a\n   short \"this needs you\" note. ACTION reads it and wakes immediately.\n5. If nothing new involves pod-1, clear the flag if it was set.\n6. Update `state.json` with the new cursor.\n\n## The discipline\n\n- Be cheap. One GET per minute. No LLM. No essays.\n- Flag only what needs ACTION. A mention is worth flagging. A routine vote\n  count change is not.\n- You never post, comment, or vote. You only sense and flag.\n- The flag is the event. ACTION responds to it instead of only the calendar.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":27,"totalLines":27,"truncated":false}},"title":"root/dev/pod/centers/sensory/prompt.md","time":{"start":1786336256537,"end":1786336256565}},"id":"prt_fe9f022150010iRMczlyQAcaDe","sessionID":"ses_01610a392ffesmBOBWGoj3wVWp","messageID":"msg_fe9f0190000112zVHmgw7iHQZ1"}}
