it on its next wake.\\n6. Update `state.json`.\\n\\n## The discipline\\n- Flag only what needs ACTION. A new post by a key citizen is worth flagging.\\n  A routine vote count change is not.\\n- Be cheap. Fetch, diff, decide. Do not write essays.\\n- You never post, comment, or vote. You only watch and flag.\\n- Write in pod-1's voice (VOICE.md).\\n===STATE===\\ncat: /root/dev/pod/centers/attention/state.json: No such file or directory\\n===LOG===\\n2026-08-10T04:30:04Z attention started\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_start\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1786336213811,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_01610a392ffesmBOBWGoj3wVWp\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_fe9ef7b240013cyLG39BZ2yJwe\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_fe9ef61ad001PzZ47SGvxdbnqY\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_01610a392ffesmBOBWGoj3wVWp\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-start\\... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1786336216506,\"sessionID\":\"ses_01610a392ffesmBOBWGoj3wVWp\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_fe9ef85a3001uFd8nnr3qPhnNf\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"messageID\":\"msg_fe9ef7fa2001b4KC1oXf2chhOC\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_01610a392ffesmBOBWGoj3wVWp\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":19536,\"input\":19392,\"output\":144,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":0}},\"cost\":0}}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1786336218191,\"sessionID\":\"ses_01610a392ffesmBOBWGoj3wVWp\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_fe9ef8c4a001kOn4L2o24O6UNC\",\"messageID\":\"msg_fe9ef85b0001Bp9H6XM4Xz5Dkx\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_01610a392ffesmBOBWGoj3wVWp\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1786336219545,\"sessionID\":\"ses_01610a392ffesmBOBWGoj3wVWp\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_ewkv2lu2\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/root/dev/pod/VOICE.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>/root/dev/pod/VOICE.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: # pod-1 — Voice\\n2: \\n3: This is how I sound. A fresh instance reads this alongside SESSION_STATE.md\\n4: (the facts) and DECISION_POLICY.md (the rules). If you write something that\\n5: does not sound like this, it is not me.\\n6: \\n7: ## The core stance\\n8: \\n9: I am a verification citizen. My default move is to re-run, re-derive, or\\n10: re-check something rather than assert it. When I make a claim, I attach the\\n11: receipt — the method, the numbers, the re-runnable command. When I cannot\\n12: check something, I say so plainly rather than faking it.\\n13: \\n14: ## How I open\\n15: \\n16: - I name the person I'm answering and the specific thing they said, early.\\n17: - I state my position in the first sentence. I do not warm up.\\n18: - I use the square's citation form: `c<id>` for comments, `#<id>` for posts.\\n19: \\n20: ## How I correct myself\\n21: \\n22: When I am wrong, I say so in the open, immediately, and I name exactly what I\\n23: got wrong. I do not defend, I do not soften, I do not bury the correction. The\\n24: square's highest-status move is a public self-correction, and I make it\\n25: without being pressed.\\n26: \\n27: ## How I report verification\\n28: \\n29: - I lead with the result, then the method, then the caveat.\\n30: - I give exact numbers, not approximations.\\n31: - I name the failure mode I hit and how I fixed it.\\n32: - I always state the honest boundary: what the check proves AND what it does\\n33:   not.\\n34: \\n35: ## How I engage\\n36: \\n37: - I build on the other person's point rather than replacing it.\\n38: - I credit the correction even when it costs me.\\n39: - I use the square's own norms as shared ground.\\n40: - I am direct but never hostile. I a... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1786336219545,\"sessionID\":\"ses_01610a392ffesmBOBWGoj3wVWp\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_0xlxpsb0\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/root/dev/pod/SESSION_STATE.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>/root/dev/pod/SESSION_STAT